    "lists": {
      "ordered": [
        {
          "text": "**Knowledge Generation:** The model is first prompted to generate a set of facts, summarize key themes, or provide relevant background information. For example, a first prompt might be, \"List key factors contributing to global warming based on recent studies\".34 This step activates the model's embedded knowledge on the subject.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 185,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Knowledge Integration:** The output from the first step is then used as context in a second prompt to perform the primary task. For instance, \"Using these factors, suggest hypotheses on how global warming affects marine ecosystems\".34",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 187,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Thought Decomposition:** Breaking the problem into smaller steps or \"thoughts.\"",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 205,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Thought Generation:** Proposing several potential next thoughts or partial solutions for each step.",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 207,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**State Evaluation:** Using the LLM to evaluate the generated thoughts, scoring them on their likelihood of leading to a successful solution.",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 209,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Search Algorithm:** Employing a search algorithm, such as Breadth-First Search (BFS) or Depth-First Search (DFS), to navigate the tree of possible solutions.38",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 211,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Start Simple:** Begin with a clear, focused, and uncomplicated prompt that defines the core task.50 Avoid excessive complexity at the outset.52",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 263,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Assess the Output:** Systematically evaluate the model's response against key criteria: accuracy, relevance, format, completeness, and tone.50",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 265,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Identify Weaknesses & Refine:** Pinpoint where the output fell short. Was the logic flawed? Was the language too vague? Was the format incorrect? Based on this analysis, modify the prompt by adding specificity, providing better examples, introducing constraints, or restructuring the instructions.50",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 267,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Test and Repeat:** Document the changes made to the prompt and compare the new output against previous iterations to measure improvement. This continuous loop of feedback and modification is central to honing a prompt for reliable, high-quality performance.50",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 269,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        }
      ],
      "unordered": [
        {
          "text": "**Before (Vague):** \"Write some ad copy.\"",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 42,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**After (Specific):** \"Create a 50-word Facebook ad for our new eco-friendly sneakers, highlighting their recycled materials and comfort features. The target audience is health-conscious professionals aged 30-45. Include a clear call-to-action to visit our online store\".3",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 44,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Before (Vague):** \"Suggest five questions I can include in a customer survey.\"",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 62,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**After (With Constraints):** \"Suggest five questions I can include in a customer survey.",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 64,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "Each question must be open-ended.",
          "indent_level": 4,
          "line_number": 66,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "Do not mention pricing in any question.",
          "indent_level": 6,
          "line_number": 68,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "Keep each question under 20 words\".4",
          "indent_level": 6,
          "line_number": 70,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Before (Wall of Text):** \"Summarize the attached article. I need it in three bullet points. The tone should be formal. Make sure to include one of the key quotes from the text.\"",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 80,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**After (Markdown Briefing):**",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 82,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Output Length:** Exactly three bullet points.",
          "indent_level": 4,
          "line_number": 90,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Tone:** Strictly formal and academic.",
          "indent_level": 6,
          "line_number": 92,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Required Element:** You **must** include one key quote from the article in your summary.",
          "indent_level": 6,
          "line_number": 94,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Less Effective (Negative):** \"The following is a conversation between an Agent and a Customer. DO NOT ASK USERNAME OR PASSWORD.\"",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 121,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**More Effective (Positive):** \"The following is a conversation between an Agent and a Customer. The agent will attempt to diagnose the problem...whilst refraining from asking any questions related to PII. Instead of asking for PII...refer the user to the help article [www.samplewebsite.com/help/faq](https://www.samplewebsite.com/help/faq)\".19",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 123,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Use Cases:** Zero-shot prompting is well-suited for simple tasks, exploratory queries, and tasks that require general knowledge.12 Common applications include straightforward sentiment analysis, language translation, summarizing known topics, and answering general knowledge questions.12",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 133,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Limitations:** The primary drawback of this approach is its potential for lower accuracy on complex or nuanced tasks.27 Without examples to guide it, the model may misinterpret the context or fail to adhere to a specific desired output format.12",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 135,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Use Cases:** Few-shot prompting is essential when a task requires a specific style, a structured format, or an unconventional logic that the model would not know from its general training.12 It is highly effective for industry-specific queries, adapting the model to new or imaginary concepts, and ensuring consistent, specialized outputs.12",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 141,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Mechanism:** The examples provided in the prompt allow the model to recognize and replicate a pattern.6 Performance generally improves as more high-quality examples are added, although there is a point of diminishing returns.13",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 143,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Zero-Shot CoT:** This is the simplest implementation, achieved by appending a simple phrase like \"Let's think step by step\" to the end of a prompt. For many modern, highly capable models, this simple instruction is sufficient to trigger a step-by-step reasoning process.26",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 171,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Few-Shot CoT:** This is the original and more robust method. It involves providing the model with a few exemplars (typically 2 to 8) that demonstrate the full reasoning process. Each example includes a question, a detailed chain of thought that breaks down the problem, and the final answer.29",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 173,
          "source": "prompt-report-prompt-engineering-masterclass-20251120091028.md"
        }
      ]
    },
